  "sourceVitestConfigDifferencesFromCapsule": [
    "The execution config narrows include to the one unchanged original test and uses a stage-local cache/output path.",
    "The source aliases, automatic JSX, feature-wall define, execArgv, timeouts, happy-dom environment annotation, offscreen-canvas setup and MutationObserver retention setup are preserved.",
    "The host-port setup is omitted because every case injects loadSnapshot and the source test hoists its own store mock; the omitted setup creates an unrelated temporary user-data directory and installs app/secret host ports.",
    "Three declared fixture seams resolve the source test's own mocked store target, the uncalled launch-session boundary, and getAgentLabel; the latter preserves codex -> Codex but is a qualification because it is called during rendering even though no assertion observes its text.",
    "All ?url asset imports resolve to deterministic stage-only URLs without reading or copying media; no assertion reads src values or image bytes, but rendered image URLs are therefore qualified.",
    "Six supplemental installed package links are separately version-checked, package-metadata hashed, full-tree hashed, and reverified because the accepted renderer helper links only react, react-dom and happy-dom."
  ],
  "dependencyClosureNote": "Exact runtime source closure for the eight Vitest-expanded original cases, plus direct shared type-contract evidence. Type-only transitive declarations erased by esbuild are not executed. Three explicit fixture seams and the asset URL seam are declared above.",
  "isolationRationale": "Runs only from a fresh .preflight capsule with stage-local cache/temp/results. The test injects loadSnapshot/runResponsibility, hoists its store mock, and does not call session launch, filesystem, service, credential, network, cloud or publication APIs."
